================================================================================
ADDITIONAL ENGINEERING-USE DISCLAIMER
================================================================================

Aquila is a software tool for pressure-transient analysis (PTA), provided
for educational, research, and engineering-decision-support purposes. The
analytical methods, correlations, and inversion routines implemented here
are documented in `docs/Aquila_Methods.pdf` and reference the peer-reviewed
petroleum-engineering literature.

The user acknowledges that:

  1. Real well-test interpretation requires qualified human judgment.
     Outputs from this tool are intended to assist, not replace, the work
     of a competent petroleum engineer.

  2. The PVT correlations (DAK, LGE, Sutton, Wichert-Aziz) and the layered-
     reservoir models are valid only within their published ranges of
     applicability. Use outside those ranges may produce non-physical
     results.

  3. No representation is made about the suitability of this software for
     any specific operational, regulatory, or commercial decision. The
     author bears no liability for decisions made on the basis of its
     output.

  4. The match between simulated and observed responses is necessary but
     not sufficient evidence of correctness; alternative interpretations
     consistent with the same data may exist.

